    &lt;/X&gt; 
  &lt;/tt:template&gt; 
&lt;/tt:transform&gt;

The transformation consists of a template temp that defines the structure
of the XML data and establishes relationships between value nodes and components of the structure. The
ST statements tt:value
and tt:copy are used to
serialize and deserialize the structure components. The reverse transformation generates the same content in the structure result as in struc1.

Description

An internal table, carrier_tab, is filled with data from the database table
SCARR and is transformed to XML using the simple transformation DEMO_ST_TABLE. The ST program is as follows:

&lt;?sap.transform simple?&gt; 
&lt;tt:transform xmlns:tt="http://www.sap.com/transformation-templates"&gt; 

  &lt;tt:root name="CARRIERS"/&gt; 
  &lt;tt:template&gt; 
    &lt;html&gt; 

      &lt;body&gt; 
        &lt;h2&gt;Carriers:&lt;/h2&gt; 

        &lt;table border="2"&gt; 
          &lt;tr&gt; 

            &lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;Id&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt; 

            &lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;Name&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt; 

            &lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;Homepage&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt; 

          &lt;/tr&gt; 
          &lt;tt:loop ref=".CARRIERS"&gt; 

            &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt; 
 
              &lt;tt:value ref="$ref.carrid"/&gt; 

              &lt;/td&gt; 
              &lt;td&gt; 

                &lt;tt:value ref="$ref.carrname"/&gt; 

              &lt;/td&gt; 
              &lt;td&gt; 

               &lt;a&gt;&lt;tt:attribute name="href" value-ref="$ref.url" /&gt; 

                 &lt;tt:value ref="$ref.url"/&gt;&lt;/a&gt; 

              &lt;/td&gt; 
            &lt;/tr&gt; 

          &lt;/tt:loop&gt; 
        &lt;/table&gt; 

      &lt;/body&gt; 
    &lt;/html&gt; 
  &lt;/tt:template&gt; 
&lt;/tt:transform&gt;

The transformation uses the ST statement tt:loop
to serialize the other internal tables row by row. HTML tags are inserted into the XML data as literals.

The result of the transformation is first shown as an XML file and then as formatted HTML data further below.

Description

Note that time_stamp is defined with the special type XSDDATETIME_Z from
ABAP Dictionary. This type ensures that a special mapping is used for the time stamp. The transformation
in question, DEMO_ST_VALUE, shows the mapping of elementary ABAP data types for date, time, and classic time stamp to XML and back.

&lt;?sap.transform simple?&gt; 
&lt;tt:transform 
  xmlns:tt="http://www.sap.com/transformation-templates"&gt; 

  &lt;tt:root name="DATE"/&gt; 
  &lt;tt:root name="TIME"/&gt; 
  &lt;tt:root name="DATETIME"/&gt; 

  &lt;tt:template&gt; 
    &lt;Date_and_Time&gt; 
      &lt;Date&gt; 

        &lt;tt:value ref="DATE"/&gt; 
      &lt;/Date&gt; 

      &lt;Time&gt; 
        &lt;tt:value ref="TIME"/&gt; 

      &lt;/Time&gt; 
      &lt;DateTime&gt; 

        &lt;tt:value ref="DATETIME"/&gt; 
      &lt;/DateTime&gt; 

    &lt;/Date_and_Time&gt; 
  &lt;/tt:template&gt; 
&lt;/tt:transform&gt;

The transformation is symmetrical.

Description

The following transformations are called in this example:

DEMO_ST_XSDANY

&lt;?sap.transform simple?&gt; 
&lt;tt:transform xmlns:tt="http://www.sap.com/transformation-templates"&gt; 

  &lt;tt:root name="ROOT"/&gt; 
  &lt;tt:template&gt; 
    &lt;node&gt; 

      &lt;tt:value ref="ROOT"/&gt; 
    &lt;/node&gt; 
  &lt;/tt:template&gt; 
&lt;/tt:transform&gt;

DEMO_ST_XSDANY_LAX

&lt;?sap.transform simple?&gt; 
&lt;tt:transform xmlns:tt="http://www.sap.com/transformation-templates"&gt; 

  &lt;tt:root name="ROOT"/&gt; 
  &lt;tt:template&gt; 
    &lt;node tt:lax="on"&gt; 

      &lt;tt:value ref="ROOT"/&gt; 
    &lt;/node&gt; 
  &lt;/tt:template&gt; 
&lt;/tt:transform&gt;

DEMO_ST_XSDANY_NO_ROOT

&lt;?sap.transform simple?&gt; 
&lt;tt:transform xmlns:tt="http://www.sap.com/transformation-templates"&gt; 

  &lt;tt:root name="ROOT"/&gt; 
  &lt;tt:template&gt; 
    &lt;node&gt; 

      &lt;tt:value option="noRootAttr" ref="ROOT"/&gt; 
    &lt;/node&gt; 
  &lt;/tt:template&gt; 
&lt;/tt:transform&gt;

DEMO_ST_XSDANY_LAX_NO_ROOT

&lt;?sap.transform simple?&gt; 
&lt;tt:transform xmlns:tt="http://www.sap.com/transformation-templates"&gt; 

  &lt;tt:root name="ROOT"/&gt; 
  &lt;tt:template&gt; 
    &lt;node tt:lax="on"&gt; 

      &lt;tt:value option="noRootAttr" ref="ROOT"/&gt; 
    &lt;/node&gt; 
  &lt;/tt:template&gt; 
&lt;/tt:transform&gt;

